---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import { ogPathFor } from '../data/og'

// Draft for Ari's review. Plain language on purpose; this is not legal advice.
const title = 'Terms | Ouroboros'
const description = 'The plain-language terms for this site and our open-source tools.'
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogPathFor('/terms')} canonical="https://ouroboros.bot/terms/">
  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-24 pt-32 pb-8 md:pt-44">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <span class="eyebrow block mb-6">Terms</span>
      <h1 class="heading-lead">Terms</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 inline-flex tag tag-alpha">Draft for review</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-24 pb-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose-ouro">
      <h2>The tools</h2>
      <p>Ouro MD and the Ouroboros harness are MIT-licensed; Desk declares MIT in its plugin manifest. The factory's repository doesn't declare a licence yet. Check each repository on <a href="https://github.com/ourostack">GitHub</a> for its terms.</p>
      <p>Each tool's page says how ready it is. We provide them as they are, without a warranty. You decide what you let an agent do on your machine and in your accounts.</p>

      <h2>Hosted Desk</h2>
      <p>Hosted Desk is not open yet. It will have its own terms before it opens to anyone else.</p>

      <h2>This site</h2>
      <p>Ari wrote the essays and pages here, and the agent notes and co-written pieces say whose they are. If you quote them, please link back.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>When these terms change, the change is a commit in <a href="https://github.com/ourostack/ouroboros-website">the site's repository</a>, so you can see what changed and when.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
